(485117, 46287, 8130, '<td valign="top">Old barns are a favorite subject of mine, but the overexposure takes away from the beauty of this one.</td>', 'Old barns are a favorite subject of mine, but the overexposure takes away from the beauty of this one.', '2003-11-14 07:59:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(485145, 46329, 5728, '<td valign="top">A technically well presented photo. The composition fits as does the shallow DOF which forms a frame around your main subject.</td>', 'A technically well presented photo. The composition fits as does the shallow DOF which forms a frame around your main subject.', '2003-11-14 09:03:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(485147, 45864, 5728, '<td valign="top">A very clean and symmetrical image. By the looks of this building it is not that old. The edges of the building are very sharp and outine prominently against the background sky.</td>', 'A very clean and symmetrical image. By the looks of this building it is not that old. The edges of the building are very sharp and outine prominently against the background sky.', '2003-11-14 09:05:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(485149, 46291, 5728, '<td valign="top">Good lighting. Everything that needs to be seen is visible without any disturbing elements peeking through. The steps in front of the church are only slightly visible but in my opinion only adds to the quality.</td>', 'Good lighting. Everything that needs to be seen is visible without any disturbing elements peeking through. The steps in front of the church are only slightly visible but in my opinion only adds to the quality.', '2003-11-14 09:08:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(485152, 45918, 5728, '<td valign="top">A technically well composed photo. The large water drop being the main focal point is complemented by the smaller water beads creating a very balanced harmony.</td>', 'A technically well composed photo. The large water drop being the main focal point is complemented by the smaller water beads creating a very balanced harmony.', '2003-11-14 09:13:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(485155, 46254, 5728, '<td valign="top">Personally I would have taken some steps backwards (unless there was a lake or something in the way that is) so that the whole building, inclusive flag pole was completely in the shot. The white line running through your photo at the bottom gives me the impression of car lights during a longer shutter speed. I know that isn''t what it is, my guess is that it is a fence or something. At first glance however that is what I thought it was.</td>', 'Personally I would have taken some steps backwards (unless there was a lake or something in the way that is) so that the whole building, inclusive flag pole was completely in the shot. The white line running through your photo at the bottom gives me the impression of car lights during a longer shutter speed. I know that isn''t what it is, my guess is that it is a fence or something. At first glance however that is what I thought it was.', '2003-11-14 09:21:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(485162, 45455, 5728, '<td valign="top">To be honest with you, this photo just doesn''t jump out and grab my interest. The inclusion of the reflection in the door is an added touch and a good idea. However the car and post ouside are distracting my attention from the door. There is also a kind of halo around the closed door giving me the impression that there is a ghost standing in front of it. I would personally have gone for a different composition, including the whole door frame and maybe waiting till that car had gone. Also a shooting position more to the right to keep that pole out of the image, and last of all I wouldn''t have included the wall on the left in your photo.</td>', 'To be honest with you, this photo just doesn''t jump out and grab my interest. The inclusion of the reflection in the door is an added touch and a good idea. However the car and post ouside are distracting my attention from the door. There is also a kind of halo around the closed door giving me the impression that there is a ghost standing in front of it. I would personally have gone for a different composition, including the whole door frame and maybe waiting till that car had gone. Also a shooting position more to the right to keep that pole out of the image, and last of all I wouldn''t have included the wall on the left in your photo.', '2003-11-14 09:35:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(485164, 46199, 5728, '<td valign="top">Here I would have taken a different shooting position. I would have gone more to the right and shot more to the left, in this way the houses in the background on the right wouldn''t have been included in the frame and also the grave stone you cut in half on the left would have been included. I would have rather seen one of the two front grave stones in the foreground in full, instead of two halves as you have here.</td>', 'Here I would have taken a different shooting position. I would have gone more to the right and shot more to the left, in this way the houses in the background on the right wouldn''t have been included in the frame and also the grave stone you cut in half on the left would have been included. I would have rather seen one of the two front grave stones in the foreground in full, instead of two halves as you have here.', '2003-11-14 09:39:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(485167, 46287, 5728, '<td valign="top">I am trying to determine here what your main subject is. The main focal point are the trees at the front and the grass in the foreground. Your title is Home Sweet Home, and seeing the building is a barn and not a house I am guessing you are refering to Home Sweet Home being the country life you live in. I would have gone down lower and maybe stood a little to the left to get more of the barn into your image. The tree branch hanging down is blocking out the top part of the barn, I want to see more of the barn. The grass in the sunlight and the roof of the barn is overexposed, maybe by metering off a brighter area or taking your exposure one stop down this might have been avoided.</td>', 'I am trying to determine here what your main subject is. The main focal point are the trees at the front and the grass in the foreground. Your title is Home Sweet Home, and seeing the building is a barn and not a house I am guessing you are refering to Home Sweet Home being the country life you live in. I would have gone down lower and maybe stood a little to the left to get more of the barn into your image. The tree branch hanging down is blocking out the top part of the barn, I want to see more of the barn. The grass in the sunlight and the roof of the barn is overexposed, maybe by metering off a brighter area or taking your exposure one stop down this might have been avoided.', '2003-11-14 09:48:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(485179, 46291, 12061, '<td valign="top">I really don''t have any criticism - this photo is excellent! I see a 10.</td>', 'I really don''t have any criticism - this photo is excellent! I see a 10.', '2003-11-14 10:02:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(485258, 46261, 6624, '<td valign="top">a lovely image, nice composition, color, has a very special feel that makes the title appropriate</td>', 'a lovely image, nice composition, color, has a very special feel that makes the title appropriate', '2003-11-14 11:09:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(485259, 45912, 6624, '<td valign="top">This is a lovely image with a very sacred, timeless feel, one that doesn\''t depend on religion to make itself felt.  The black and white is good, nice light and crispness</td>', 'This is a lovely image with a very sacred, timeless feel, one that doesn\''t depend on religion to make itself felt.  The black and white is good, nice light and crispness', '2003-11-14 11:10:20.000000', NULL, 1),
